# The family root layer (pibase) this checkout is pinned to.
#
# One file on purpose. The same decision is needed in four places - the commit the
# source route fetches (scripts/fetch_pibase.ps1), the version the Conan recipe
# requires (conanfile.py), the range the installed package config accepts
# (src/piplugin/cmake/pipluginConfig.cmake.in, filled in by
# src/piplugin/CMakeLists.txt), and CI, which reads the commit from here - and
# four copies of a pin are four pins that drift.
#
# commit   the full 40-character object id of a commit in
#          https://gitee.com/Aeroscis/pibase.git (mirrored on GitHub). Full, not
#          abbreviated: a shortened id cannot be fetched by itself, which is what
#          CI does (`git fetch --depth 1 origin <commit>`) and what the local
#          script checks out. pibase has no tags yet, so a commit is the only
#          stable pin; when it starts tagging, this becomes a tag and nothing
#          else has to move.
# version  the version that commit declares - scripts/fetch_pibase.ps1 checks the
#          two against each other, so this file cannot claim one version while
#          pinning a commit that declares another.
#          It also carries the compatibility policy: piplugin accepts the pinned
#          version and later fixes in the same minor (0.1.0 up to but excluding
#          0.2.0), because the family's rule is that a patch release only fixes
#          while a minor release may rename things (pibase README, Versioning).

commit=65de807612debb4616c0e607be6450a6c52de7e5
version=0.1.0
